ction":"ICP-OES","method_description":"To measure Lipophilicity, log Po/w, the shake-flask method was used to obtain the amounts of each Pt complex in Water - Octanol [18]. 10 mg of Pt complex solved in 0.3 mL of water, pre-saturated with octanol, was incubated overnight at room temperature. After centrifuging, 0.3 mL pre-saturated octanol was added to supernatants, and the two-phase mixtures were kept shaking for 1 h to obtain the partition equilibrium, centrifugation was separately done and the Pt content in each phase was measured by ICP-OES. This data was obtained in triplicate. Table 1 shows the average log Po/w value."}]}